     The ccaapp__iiooccttllss__lliimmiitt() and ccaapp__iiooccttllss__ggeett() system calls will fail if:

     [EBADF]            The _f_d argument is not a valid descriptor.

     [EFAULT]           The _c_m_d_s argument points at an invalid address.

     [ENOSYS]           The running kernel was compiled without ooppttiioonnss
                        CCAAPPAABBIILLIITTYY__MMOODDEE.

     The ccaapp__iiooccttllss__lliimmiitt() system call may also return the following errors:

     [EINVAL]           The _n_c_m_d_s argument is greater than _2_5_6.

